// `fantasy-dungeon` — the REFERENCE asset plugin (Asset-Plugins RFC Phase 2,
// labelle-engine#725 §use-case-2 / labelle-assembler#576). A vendor-style
// "full plugin" a game attaches by one `.plugins` entry to get a whole
// dungeon content kit — bundled packs, plugin-level art, and provenance —
// with ZERO manual `.resources` edits in the consuming project.
//
// What it exercises:
//   - `.packs` — two packs BUNDLED at `plugin/packs/<name>/` (`tiles` +
//     `props`). Each is discovered as a first-class pack and flows through the
//     SAME machinery (copy, scan, `pack__` namespacing, resource merge, script
//     wiring) as a game-local pack.
//   - `.resources` — a PLUGIN-LEVEL atlas (`banner`) the plugin ships directly,
//     merged as `fantasy_dungeon__banner` and copied into
//     `packs/fantasy_dungeon/assets/…` — namespaced exactly like a pack's.
//   - `.license` / `.author` — provenance metadata for a shipped/sold plugin,
//     surfaced by `labelle plugins`.
//
// The `tiles` pack also ships a small generator script — proving the RFC's
// "a map generator is just an ordinary script; tiles are entities, tilesets
// are just atlases" claim with no new engine machinery.
.{
    .name = "fantasy_dungeon",
    .manifest_version = 1,
    .packs = .{ "tiles", "props" },
    .resources = .{
        .{ .name = "banner", .json = "assets/banner.json", .texture = "assets/banner.png" },
    },
    .license = "CC0-1.0",
    .author = "LaBelle Toolkit",
}
